# Cable Web — local development settings.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then fill in what you need
#
# .env is gitignored. NEVER commit real keys.
# Production values live in deploy/config.env (also gitignored) and are pushed to
# Azure by deploy/provision.sh — API keys go across as Container App *secrets*,
# not plain environment variables.

# ── Local storage + auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AUTH_MODE=local
COOKIE_SECURE=false
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./local.db
DATA_DIR=./_data
UPLOAD_DIR=./_data/uploads

# ── Optional: AI reading of module datasheets ────────────────────────────────
# Leave the key blank and the feature is OFF — the app then identifies modules
# only against the CEC database, exactly as it does today.
#
# It is called ONLY when the CEC database cannot identify a module by name AND
# cannot identify it by its nameplate values — i.e. a genuinely unknown panel or
# a scan with no readable text. Its answer is a suggestion the engineer confirms;
# once saved to the module library, that module never needs another API call.

OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides:
#   AI_MODEL     defaults to gpt-4o (openai) / claude-opus-5 (anthropic)
#   AI_PROVIDER  only needed to force one when several keys are set
#   AI_DATASHEET_EXTRACTION=false  kill switch, even with a key present
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o
# AI_PROVIDER=openai
# AI_DATASHEET_EXTRACTION=true

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
